Goal: Use Ansible modules to check and manage your 2 EC2 servers.

You already have:

WSL
 |
 | Ansible
 |
 +---- EC2-1 (web1)
 |
 +---- EC2-2 (web2)

And your directory:

~/ansible-ec2-lab/
├── ansible.cfg
└── inventory

Step 1 — Check both servers

First:

cd ~/ansible-ec2-lab

Run:

web1 | SUCCESS => {
    "ping": "pong"
}

web2 | SUCCESS => {
    "ping": "pong"
}

Step 2 — Check disk usage

Run:

ansible all -m command -a "df -h /"

You'll get the root filesystem information from both servers.

For example:

Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use%
/dev/root        8G   3G    5G   38%

Step 3 — Use the shell module

Now let's try another module.

ansible all -m shell -a "uptime && df -h /"

Here we're running two commands:

uptime

and:

df -h /

The shell module is useful when you need shell features or multiple commands.
ansible all -m ping
